The desk merged reports with similar subjects, but matching subjects does not establish a common cause. The underlying data and tenant settings distinguish a shared parser that reads dates month first from a booking-v3 hint that instructs users to enter dates month first while the form reads them in the tenant's locale.

## Reports by cause

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table uses unique report IDs and tenant settings. Intake tags are guesses, not the cause. The desk notes identify reports that read as a one-day move; the current classifier still files them by tenant and channel. Investigate their underlying cause before treating the table's attribution as conclusive.

## The queue over time

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The export is a snapshot: received dates and merge dates are different events. Do not infer that every report was received when the desk merged it.

## Duplicates

Match reports by established cause, not subject alone. Keep uncertain reports separate until the tenant and route are known. The accepted decision record remains historical; replace it through a new decision if the desk adopts this rule.

